1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Most buyers decide whether to make an
offer based on the price and the photos.

2
00:00:05,220 --> 00:00:08,140
The ones who get into trouble
later are usually the

3
00:00:08,140 --> 00:00:11,600
ones who didn't ask a handful
of basic questions first.

4
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:14,250
In this video, I'm going
to give you four questions

5
00:00:14,250 --> 00:00:18,360
to ask before you offer on any
property, residential or commercial.

6
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:20,850
I'm Jake, the founder of Calibre Acquire.

7
00:00:20,850 --> 00:00:24,210
I've worked in property for 14
years and transacted on over £80

8
00:00:24,210 --> 00:00:28,230
million worth of commercial property
investments in the past year alone.

9
00:00:28,230 --> 00:00:30,910
I help investors get out of
underperforming property assets

10
00:00:30,910 --> 00:00:33,080
and into ones that actually
work harder for them.

11
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:36,060
Question one is the tenant's strength.

12
00:00:36,060 --> 00:00:38,520
Who's paying the rent,
and how secure is it?

13
00:00:38,520 --> 00:00:41,070
If the property is tenanted,
you're not just buying a

14
00:00:41,070 --> 00:00:44,200
building, you're buying the
tenant's ability to keep paying.

15
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:47,660
Ask how long they've been in
occupation, whether they've ever

16
00:00:47,660 --> 00:00:50,600
missed a payment, and how
long is left on the lease.

17
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:54,160
The asking price can often
look the same and reflect the

18
00:00:54,160 --> 00:00:57,720
same yield, but it can cause
issues further down the line.

19
00:00:57,720 --> 00:01:00,890
If you're considering a property
and want to stress test it within

20
00:01:00,890 --> 00:01:05,710
a few minutes, I've built calculators for
mixed-use, HMO and single residential

21
00:01:05,710 --> 00:01:08,470
deals, so you can put in the
real numbers and see what a

22
00:01:08,470 --> 00:01:11,720
deal actually returns, not just
what it looks like on the surface.

23
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:12,790
Completely free.

24
00:01:12,790 --> 00:01:15,680
Comment the word send below, or
use the link below to get access.

25
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:17,570
Question two, the true cost.

26
00:01:17,570 --> 00:01:21,090
What does this actually cost
beyond the purchase price?

27
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:24,830
Service charge, ground rent,
repairs, planning constraints.

28
00:01:24,830 --> 00:01:27,850
These don't show up in the
headline figure, but they

29
00:01:27,850 --> 00:01:31,040
affect your return every year
that you hold onto the property.

30
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:35,120
Ask for the last three years' service
charge accounts if there's one in place.

31
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:38,480
Ask whether any major works
are planned or already agreed.

32
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:41,270
A property that looks
cheaper on paper can end up

33
00:01:41,270 --> 00:01:43,600
costing a lot more once
these are factored in.

34
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:46,200
Question three, the vendor's motivation.

35
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:48,160
Why is the vendor actually selling?

36
00:01:48,160 --> 00:01:51,680
This shapes how the negotiation
goes and what you might uncover.

37
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:57,100
A vendor selling because of probate,
retirement or a change in circumstances

38
00:01:57,100 --> 00:02:00,680
behaves differently to one selling because
the property has become a problem.

39
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:03,460
It's not always something you'll
get a straight answer to,

40
00:02:03,460 --> 00:02:06,600
but it's worth asking your agent
or solicitor what they know.

41
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:10,720
The reason behind a sale often explains
things the listing itself won't.

42
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:13,520
Question four is the exit strategy.

43
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:15,320
Who would buy this from me later?

44
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:19,080
Before you buy it, it's worth knowing
what your future buyer looks like.

45
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:22,760
A property with broad appeal,
good location, flexible use,

46
00:02:22,760 --> 00:02:25,800
no unusual lease structure,
is easier to sell on.

47
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:30,440
A highly specific asset could be
harder to move, even at a fair price.

48
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:33,160
This doesn't mean you need
to plan an exit on day one.

49
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:36,040
But if you can't picture who'd
want to buy the property in

50
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:39,440
five or 10 years, that's worth
considering before you make an offer.

51
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:43,030
None of these questions guarantee
a good outcome on their own.

52
00:02:43,030 --> 00:02:45,830
But asking them before you
offer, rather than after

53
00:02:45,830 --> 00:02:48,640
you've exchanged, puts you
in a much stronger position.

54
